o us gets loving care  and hopefully gets a pathway to a real  strong forever home wow well thank you  so much for all that you guys do at the  animal foundation um how can people help  the first thing you can do is you can  adopt um summer is coming it's very busy  and so we're seeing a lot more animals  in the shelter  that also means that there are hundreds  of animals that you can meet and open  your heart to and take into your home  a lot of them  already  more senior animals a little bit older  that have some training that have been  around  kids and uh different folks so that you  know that they'll be an instant  wonderful family member there are some  others that are going to need a little  bit more of a loving touch  the second thing is fostering  if you can foster a pet if you're not  ready to adopt  we really would like to get as many pets  out of the shelter quickly as possible  and into kind of a home environment and  fostering is just one of the many ways  that people can volunteer with us  we have a ton of volunteer jobs in the  shelter everything from administrative  things to working with our behavior and  enrichment team to being a part of that  adoption process finally since we're a  non-profit donations are very important  wow i know for sure hillary someone out  there is watching and wants to help  after that explanation so um how can how  can they do that is there a website or  somewhere they should go to find more  information  yes we have a website that's full of  resources it's  animalfoundation.com you can find out  how to volunteer you can donate you can  browse all of our adoptable animals and  hopefully find your next forever friend  here's to the next 50 years of both of  your organizations thank you so much  thank you thank you  thank you again to southwest medical for  sponsoring that segment and being one of  our community pride partners
 

